      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Mononuclear Dy complex 2c shows room-temperature χT close to one isolated Dy3+, a decrease of χT on cooling, magnetic anisotropy (nonsuperimposable M vs H/T, no saturation at 7 T), and slow magnetization relaxation. No χ″ peak is observed in zero dc field, but SMM behavior appears under 2000 Oe: Cole–Cole plots (3–9.5 K) fit a generalized Debye model (α = 0.03–0.21) and above 7.5 K an Orbach process gives Ueff = 67 K and τ0 = 1.68 × 10−7 s. Two χ″ peaks at higher frequencies suggest a possible multiple-relaxation process.",
