        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Mononuclear [Dy(nma)2]+ complex 3 (two crystallographically independent Dy units) shows room-temperature χT close to one Dy3+, a decrease of χT on cooling, magnetic anisotropy, and slow relaxation. No χ″ peak in zero dc field; under 2000 Oe, Cole–Cole plots (2–12 K) show a double-ridge structure. Arrhenius analysis gives Ueff = 16 K (τ0 = 1.0 × 10−5 s) and 47 K (τ0 = 4.6 × 10−6 s) for the low- and high-temperature domains. Deviation below 7 K is ascribed to a direct process replacing thermally activated reversal; relatively large τ0 is attributed to QTM.",
